# Third-party notices

Not-Everything itself is MIT-licensed (see `LICENSE`). The app and the `not-everything` command are built with the open-source crates below, whose licences ask for their notices to be kept with every copy. The app shows this text in its About panel and keeps it in its bundle; `not-everything -licenses` prints it.

This file is written by `scripts/third-party-notices.sh` (cargo-about) from `Cargo.lock`. Don't edit it by hand; run the script after any dependency change.

