## Copyright notices for crates published without one

These crates were published under the MIT licence without a copyright line, so the MIT text above that lists them shows the licence's placeholder. Their projects name the copyright holders as:

- The objc2 crates (`objc2`, `objc2-encode`, `objc2-foundation`, `objc2-app-kit`, `objc2-core-foundation`, `objc2-service-management`): Mads Marquart and the objc2 contributors (https://github.com/madsmtm/objc2, whose `LICENSE-MIT.txt` names Mads Marquart).
- The windows crates (`windows-link`, `windows-sys`, `windows-targets` and the `windows_*` target crates, built only for Windows): Microsoft Corporation (https://github.com/microsoft/windows-rs, whose `license-mit` reads "Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.").
